! vfl_internal_operand.strap -- A VFL OPERAND IN AN INTERNAL REGISTER
! ($L) WAITS FOR THE E-BOX.  Built 2026-11-17 with StretchCore's
! headReady (intWait), StretchIBox's vflInternalFetch and StretchTiming's
! vflInternalOperandClocks (docs/atlas_oracle.md, "Closing the
! residuals" item 10).
!
! THE SOURCE.  Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-20 (PDF 38, read in the
! image): "The I-box, upon decoding an instruction whose fetch operand is
! an internal register, uses the LAAR to store the internal operand
! address. This is because the needed operand is not available during
! the decoding stage ..."  "(By an internal operand address is meant
! address 3, or an address between 5 and 12 inclusive.)"  Perf. Char.
! Vol. 2's forwarding pages print the INTERNL column (operand at 8.0,
! PDF 114) 4 clocks over EXTERNL: L (BU,64,8) on PDF 147 is 9.60 us
! internal against 8.40 forwarded from memory.
!
! THE BODY.  The accumulator is loaded with (16)0123456789ABCDEF; eight
! L(BU,64,8) from 8.0 ($L, the accumulator's left word: each reloads the
! same value) and then eight from memory (the external control inside
! the deck: the wait does not apply to them); RES gets the accumulator.
!
! MEASURED, 2026-11-17 (CYCLES in run_tests.sh's run line).
!   the model as of this deck .......................... CYCLES 552
!   OBSERVED INJECTION, reverted from a saved copy checked with cmp:
!   - vflInternalFetch forced False ..................... CYCLES 520
!   Nothing else failed (PC and RES pass).
! The control is decks/fp_internal_operand.strap (an FP internal
! operand, intWait's other half), whose CYCLES (208) did not move under the
! injection.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

START   L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        ST(BU,64,8), RES

PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, (8)2200.0

VAL     DD(BU,64,8), (16)0123456789ABCDEF
RES     DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
